    {
      "id": 36777,
      "name": "Sona8",
      "slug": "sona8",
      "former_names": [],
      "small_logo_thumb_url": "https://bookface-images.s3.amazonaws.com/small_logos/bbb7f2bc6b3848168f970a704b24b37c2b125f25.png",
      "website": "https://sona8.com",
      "all_locations": "San Francisco, CA, USA",
      "long_description": "Sona8 is a voice agent that talks to every employee in a company about how their work gets done.\r\n\r\nEach employee gets a link and talks to the agent for about 20 minutes. The agent asks follow-up questions, for example why a step is still done by hand or who else is involved. From the conversations we build process maps and a list of the problems\r\npeople described, sorted by site and team.\r\n\r\nThat is the start. We then stay on through the implementation. After each initiative is rolled out, the agent goes back to the employees involved and asks whether it was implemented and what changed in their daily work. The transformation team sees this\r\nafter every rollout step.\r\n\r\nThe result is a project management office that has talked to every employee. That context did not exist before, because nobody had the time to collect it.\r\n\r\nConsulting firms use it to gather ideas at the start of an engagement instead. Transformation and corporate development teams use it to guide the execution of strategic transformation.",
      "one_liner": "Voice agents that talk to employees enabling transformations ",
      "team_size": 4,
      "highlight_black": false,
      "highlight_latinx": false,
      "highlight_women": false,
